{"cells": [{"cell_type": "markdown", "id": "8de9ee7d", "metadata": {}, "source": ["# Paper Metadata\n", "\n", "One tidy row per paper. Primary key: `paper_id` (OpenAlex `W\u2026`, shared with every other paper output in\n", "`notebook/paper/output/`).\n", "\n", "## Raw data (directory & structure)\n", "```\n", "Data/SciSciNet_v2/sciscinet_papers_fos.parquet   # paperid(W), year, doctype, reference_count, citation_count, FoS_0, FoS_rep\n", "E:/Dawoon Jeong/Data/scisci_intermediate/main_primary/paper_metadata.sqlite  # papers(paper_id[MAG int], year, journal_id)\n", "E:/Dawoon Jeong/Data/MAG/mag/Journals.txt        # JournalId, ..., DisplayName(col3)   -> journal name\n", "E:/Dawoon Jeong/Data/MAG/mag/PaperAuthorAffiliations.txt  # PaperId, AuthorId, ...      -> author_list (HEAVY 51 GB, optional)\n", "```\n", "`paperid` = `W{n}` where `n` is the MAG `paper_id`; MAG `journal_id` joins to `Journals.txt`.\n", "\n", "## Output columns\n", "`paper_id, year, ref_count, journal, author_list, FoS_0, FoS_rep` (+ `doctype`).\n", "- `journal` = MAG journal DisplayName (via `journal_id`); `FoS_0`/`FoS_rep` = level-0 field(s).\n", "- `author_list` = `;`-joined MAG `AuthorId` ordered by author sequence \u2014 **only built if `RUN_AUTHORS=True`**\n", "  (a 51 GB scan of `PaperAuthorAffiliations.txt`); otherwise left null.\n", "\n", "Output \u2192 `notebook/paper/output/paper_metadata.parquet`.\n", "\n", "> Note: 249.8M papers. Journal join is done with DuckDB out-of-core. The author scan is heavy and off by default."]}, {"cell_type": "code", "execution_count": 1, "id": "642a32dc", "metadata": {"execution": {"iopub.execute_input": "2026-08-26T21:58:44.403737Z", "iopub.status.busy": "2026-08-26T21:58:44.403737Z", "iopub.status.idle": "2026-08-26T21:58:44.809942Z", "shell.execute_reply": "2026-08-26T21:58:44.809942Z"}}, "outputs": [{"name": "stdout", "output_type": "stream", "text": ["ROOT: C:\\Users\\jdwoo\\OneDrive\\Desktop\\Research\\Science of Science\n"]}], "source": ["import pyarrow.parquet as pq\n", "import os, sys, gc, time\n", "import numpy as np, pandas as pd\n", "sys.path.insert(0, '/project/jevans/Dawoon/Science of Science/OpenAlex')\n", "import oa_common as oa\n", "ROOT = oa.BASE; OUT = oa.OUT\n", "print('snapshot:', oa.ROOT)\n", "OUT_FP = f'{OUT}/paper_metadata.parquet'\n", "# MAG's Journals.txt + paper_metadata.sqlite + sciscinet_papers_fos.parquet are all replaced by\n", "# two caches built once from the snapshot: primary_locations x sources, and topics x topics.csv.gz.\n", "RUN_AUTHORS = False   # author_list from works_au_affs_fixed.csv.gz (38 GB gzip scan) \u2014 off by default\n", "# Everything below is fed by notebook/referenced_works_w_year.ipynb: it writes the per-work\n", "# map (year + source) and the edge table with both years and both source ids, and\n", "# oa.load_graph() / oa.load_csr() / oa.build_journal() read those instead of re-walking\n", "# renli's tree. Build it once before running this notebook.\n", "assert oa.have_consolidated(), (\n", "    'run notebook/referenced_works_w_year.ipynb first \u2014 it builds the map and edge table')\n", "oa.summary()"]}, {"cell_type": "markdown", "id": "94770774", "metadata": {}, "source": ["## 1. journal_id -> journal name map (MAG); paper -> journal_id (sqlite)"]}, {"cell_type": "code", "execution_count": 2, "id": "bc787f93", "metadata": {"execution": {"iopub.execute_input": "2026-08-26T21:58:44.811218Z", "iopub.status.busy": "2026-08-26T21:58:44.811218Z", "iopub.status.idle": "2026-08-26T22:06:52.486376Z", "shell.execute_reply": "2026-08-26T22:06:52.486376Z"}}, "outputs": [{"name": "stdout", "output_type": "stream", "text": ["paper->journal rows: 90,282,328\n"]}, {"name": "stdout", "output_type": "stream", "text": ["CPU times: total: 1min 57s\n", "Wall time: 8min 7s\n"]}], "source": ["%%time\n", "# 1. work -> journal (primary_locations x sources.csv.gz), work -> field (topics x topics.csv.gz)\n", "oa.build_journal()\n", "oa.build_fos()\n", "jr = pd.read_parquet(oa.JOURNAL_PQ, columns=['work_id', 'journal', 'is_journal'])\n", "fs = pd.read_parquet(oa.FOS_PQ,     columns=['work_id', 'FoS_rep', 'FoS_0', 'domain'])\n", "print(f'journal rows {len(jr):,} | FoS rows {len(fs):,}')"]}, {"cell_type": "markdown", "id": "8c56d921", "metadata": {}, "source": ["## 2. Assemble base fields (DuckDB, out-of-core) + join journal"]}, {"cell_type": "code", "execution_count": 3, "id": "5132e850", "metadata": {"execution": {"iopub.execute_input": "2026-08-26T22:06:52.487378Z", "iopub.status.busy": "2026-08-26T22:06:52.487378Z", "iopub.status.idle": "2026-08-26T22:07:19.437482Z", "shell.execute_reply": "2026-08-26T22:07:19.437482Z"}}, "outputs": [{"name": "stdout", "output_type": "stream", "text": ["base written -> C:\\Users\\jdwoo\\OneDrive\\Desktop\\Research\\Science of Science\\notebook\\paper\\output\\paper_metadata.parquet\n"]}, {"name": "stdout", "output_type": "stream", "text": ["        n  with_journal  with_fos\n", "249803279      85374037 249785313\n", "CPU times: total: 2min 57s\n", "Wall time: 26.9 s\n"]}], "source": ["%%time\n", "# 2. Base fields from works/works + a reference count from works/referenced_works.\n", "#    OpenAlex works carries no reference_count column, so it is counted from the edge list.\n", "import pyarrow.parquet as pq\n", "# The reference count comes from the consolidated edge table when it exists: one row per\n", "# edge, so a value_counts on work_id IS the count, and no second walk over\n", "# works/referenced_works is needed. Partitions are aligned, so the pairing below is a local\n", "# join, never a shuffle.\n", "REF = oa.ref_parts() if oa.have_consolidated() else oa.parts('referenced_works')\n", "REF_COL = 'work_id'\n", "frames = []\n", "wp = oa.parts('works')\n", "assert len(wp) == len(REF), 'works and edge partitions must line up'\n", "for i, (fw, fr) in enumerate(zip(wp, REF)):\n", "    w = pq.read_table(fw, columns=['id', 'publication_year', 'type', 'cited_by_count',\n", "                                   'is_retracted']).to_pandas()\n", "    w = w.rename(columns={'id': 'work_id', 'publication_year': 'year', 'type': 'doctype'})\n", "    w['work_id'] = oa.norm_id(w['work_id'])\n", "    r = pq.read_table(fr, columns=[REF_COL]).to_pandas()\n", "    rc = oa.norm_id(r[REF_COL]).value_counts().rename('ref_count')\n", "    frames.append(w.join(rc, on='work_id'))\n", "    del w, r, rc\n", "    if (i + 1) % 300 == 0:\n", "        print(f'  {i+1}/{len(wp)} partitions', flush=True)\n", "base = pd.concat(frames, ignore_index=True); del frames; gc.collect()\n", "base['ref_count'] = base['ref_count'].fillna(0).astype('int32')\n", "print(f'works: {len(base):,}')"]}, {"cell_type": "markdown", "id": "7152242d", "metadata": {}, "source": ["## 3. (optional) author_list from MAG PaperAuthorAffiliations \u2014 heavy"]}, {"cell_type": "code", "execution_count": 4, "id": "7c85c91d", "metadata": {"execution": {"iopub.execute_input": "2026-08-26T22:07:19.440550Z", "iopub.status.busy": "2026-08-26T22:07:19.439558Z", "iopub.status.idle": "2026-08-26T22:07:19.446061Z", "shell.execute_reply": "2026-08-26T22:07:19.445557Z"}}, "outputs": [{"name": "stdout", "output_type": "stream", "text": ["RUN_AUTHORS=False -> author_list skipped (column absent). Set True to build it.\n"]}], "source": ["%%time\n", "# 3. Assemble and save\n", "meta = (base.merge(jr, on='work_id', how='left')\n", "             .merge(fs, on='work_id', how='left')\n", "             .rename(columns={'work_id': 'paper_id'}))\n", "if RUN_AUTHORS:\n", "    # works_au_affs_fixed.csv.gz is 38 GB compressed and its work_id/author_id are URLs.\n", "    import gzip\n", "    from collections import defaultdict\n", "    auth = defaultdict(list)\n", "    for ch in pd.read_csv(f'{oa.ROOT}/works_au_affs_fixed.csv.gz',\n", "                          usecols=['work_id', 'author_id', 'author_position_int'],\n", "                          dtype=str, chunksize=5_000_000):\n", "        ch = ch.dropna(subset=['author_id'])\n", "        for w, a in zip(oa.norm_id(ch['work_id']), oa.norm_id(ch['author_id'])):\n", "            auth[w].append(a)\n", "    ad = pd.DataFrame({'paper_id': list(auth), 'author_list': [';'.join(v) for v in auth.values()]})\n", "    meta = meta.merge(ad, on='paper_id', how='left')\n", "else:\n", "    meta['author_list'] = pd.NA\n", "    print('RUN_AUTHORS=False -> author_list left null')\n", "meta = meta[['paper_id', 'year', 'doctype', 'ref_count', 'journal', 'is_journal',\n", "             'author_list', 'FoS_0', 'FoS_rep', 'domain', 'cited_by_count', 'is_retracted']]\n", "meta.to_parquet(OUT_FP, index=False)\n", "print(f'WROTE {OUT_FP}  ({len(meta):,} rows, {len(meta.columns)} cols)')\n", "print(f\"  with journal {meta.journal.notna().mean()*100:.1f}%  |  with FoS \"\n", "      f\"{meta.FoS_rep.notna().mean()*100:.1f}%\")"]}, {"cell_type": "markdown", "id": "4ee44203", "metadata": {}, "source": ["## 4. Example"]}, {"cell_type": "code", "execution_count": 5, "id": "18e49d34", "metadata": {"execution": {"iopub.execute_input": "2026-08-26T22:07:19.447072Z", "iopub.status.busy": "2026-08-26T22:07:19.447072Z", "iopub.status.idle": "2026-08-26T22:09:57.422852Z", "shell.execute_reply": "2026-08-26T22:09:57.418850Z"}}, "outputs": [{"data": {"text/html": ["<div>\n", "<style scoped>\n", "    .dataframe tbody tr th:only-of-type {\n", "        vertical-align: middle;\n", "    }\n", "\n", "    .dataframe tbody tr th {\n", "        vertical-align: top;\n", "    }\n", "\n", "    .dataframe thead th {\n", "        text-align: right;\n", "    }\n", "</style>\n", "<table border=\"1\" class=\"dataframe\">\n", "  <thead>\n", "    <tr style=\"text-align: right;\">\n", "      <th></th>\n", "      <th>paper_id</th>\n", "      <th>year</th>\n", "      <th>doctype</th>\n", "      <th>ref_count</th>\n", "      <th>FoS_0</th>\n", "      <th>FoS_rep</th>\n", "      <th>journal</th>\n", "    </tr>\n", "  </thead>\n", "  <tbody>\n", "    <tr>\n", "      <th>0</th>\n", "      <td>W1496852943</td>\n", "      <td>1974</td>\n", "